  greetings:
  - Evenin'.
  - You're on my land, Detective.
  aboutSelf: Corn. Sixty years of corn. It don't ask questions.
  aboutTown: Town's fine. People are fine. You should go home.
  seenAnythingStrange: Something walks my rows at night. The corn moves against the wind. I don't go out there after dark no more.
  foundersDay: Wet. Mae's cherry pie took it. Crane went on about weeds in the wheat.
  gossip:
  - title: About Irene Vance
    response: Irene collects moths. Pins 'em to boards. House is full of 'em. Harmless.
  - title: About Silas Thorne
    response: Silas has a scar through his left eyebrow. Bar fight in Amarillo. Proud of it, too.
  - title: About Nell Hollis
    response: Nell's left eye's always been small. Squints like she's aiming at you.
